Third-party data and assets
---------------------------

Worlds generated by Arnis are built from third-party data, and Arnis bundles
map assets and 3D models made by their authors. Each keeps its own license and
its attribution must be preserved.

The full list of sources, authors and licenses is kept in one place, so it does
not drift: open "License and Credits" in the app, or read src/gui/js/license.js.


Modifications in this fork
---------------------------

This is a fork of the above project, maintained by monlum58
(https://github.com/monlum58/arnis), under the same Apache License,
Version 2.0. Per section 4(b) of that license, this notice records that
files in this fork have been changed from the original.

Summary of changes (see the fork's git history and README.md for detail):
  - Bounded-memory large-area generation: the elevation pipeline
    (raw fetch, terrain post-processing, Gaussian blur) is backed by
    disk-mapped storage instead of always-resident memory, so
    metro-scale bounding boxes (~2000 km2, verified) no longer require
    RAM proportional to area.
  - Overpass query tiling for large bounding boxes, merged by OSM id.
  - `--name` CLI flag for naming a generated Java Edition world.

None of the above changes what a generated world looks like for any area
that already worked before this fork's changes (verified block-for-block).
